{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00558",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.36,
      "end_seconds": 5.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Good morning. Mr. Kowalczyk? Did I get that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.03,
      "end_seconds": 14.37,
      "duration_seconds": 8.34,
      "text": "Close enough, it's Ko-VAL-chick. But the grandkids call me Pop-Pop, so call me Gene, whatever's easiest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.12,
      "end_seconds": 20.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Gene it is. And I see you've brought someone with you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 22.28,
      "end_seconds": 30.6,
      "duration_seconds": 8.32,
      "text": "I'm Tanya, one of the carers at Maplewood. I've looked after Gene for about two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.79,
      "end_seconds": 37.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Welcome, Tanya. Gene, what brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.08,
      "end_seconds": 48.76,
      "duration_seconds": 8.68,
      "text": "This wheezing, doctor. It's mostly at night, and again first thing in the morning. Sounds like a squeaky gate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 50.01,
      "end_seconds": 61.73,
      "duration_seconds": 11.72,
      "text": "I can hear it from the hall. Around four, usually. I look in and he's sitting up on the edge of the bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.95,
      "end_seconds": 70.74,
      "duration_seconds": 7.79,
      "text": "That must be wearing on both of you. How long has it been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.08,
      "end_seconds": 83.27,
      "duration_seconds": 10.19,
      "text": "About six weeks. It started around the time the lawn crew did their last cut of the season. Funny what you remember."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.45,
      "end_seconds": 88.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Does anything bring it on, or ease it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.5,
      "end_seconds": 98.48,
      "duration_seconds": 7.98,
      "text": "Cold air makes it worse. Sitting up on two pillows helps, and a warm shower."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.89,
      "end_seconds": 105.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "What about during the day? Any shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.01,
      "end_seconds": 119.55,
      "duration_seconds": 12.54,
      "text": "On the stairs, yes. I get puffed halfway up to the second floor. I used to take them in one go carrying a laundry basket."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.38,
      "end_seconds": 124.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "And do you cough at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.42,
      "end_seconds": 131.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "A dry cough, a little tickle, mostly when I lie down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.87,
      "end_seconds": 146.22,
      "duration_seconds": 13.35,
      "text": "Thank you. Now I'm going to ask about a few things you may not have. Any fever, chest pain, swelling in your legs, or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.18,
      "end_seconds": 158.16,
      "duration_seconds": 10.98,
      "text": "No, none of those. Thank goodness. My buddy Walt had a chest scare last spring and it frightened us all half to death."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.65,
      "end_seconds": 167.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "I'm glad you're clear of those. What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.69,
      "end_seconds": 179.64,
      "duration_seconds": 9.95,
      "text": "Lisinopril, 10 milligrams once a day. Metformin, 500 milligrams twice a day. Tanya, what's the third one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 180.4,
      "end_seconds": 185.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Atorvastatin, 20 milligrams at bedtime. I do the pill cups."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.52,
      "end_seconds": 191.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Perfect. Now, do you have any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.14,
      "end_seconds": 204.58,
      "duration_seconds": 11.44,
      "text": "Shellfish. I'm allergic to shellfish, it gives me hives. I found that out at my niece's wedding, after the shrimp cocktail. She still brings it up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.93,
      "end_seconds": 213.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "Hives from shellfish, noted. Are there any other health conditions I should have on the list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.04,
      "end_seconds": 223.89,
      "duration_seconds": 8.85,
      "text": "High blood pressure, type 2 diabetes, and high cholesterol. That's the holy trinity at my age."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.22,
      "end_seconds": 229.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "And any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.83,
      "end_seconds": 238.7,
      "duration_seconds": 7.87,
      "text": "Knee replacement in 2015, and my gallbladder came out about eight years ago. The knee's a champ."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.95,
      "end_seconds": 246.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Good to hear. Does any lung trouble run in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.61,
      "end_seconds": 255.0,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "My mother had asthma. She kept an old inhaler in every coat pocket."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.25,
      "end_seconds": 260.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Interesting. Have you ever smoked, Gene?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.47,
      "end_seconds": 271.11,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "A pack a day for years. I smoked until about twenty years ago, then my wife made me quit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.36,
      "end_seconds": 278.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "Good for her. And where do you live these days?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.31,
      "end_seconds": 287.42,
      "duration_seconds": 8.11,
      "text": "I live at Maplewood, the care home, third floor. Best part is the bingo on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.38,
      "end_seconds": 294.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Ha, I hope you win. Any problems with your stomach or bowels?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.86,
      "end_seconds": 299.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "No, regular as clockwork."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.19,
      "end_seconds": 307.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Good. Let me check your numbers now, and then listen to your chest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.75,
      "end_seconds": 329.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.84,
      "text": "Blood pressure 138 over 84. Pulse 82. Breathing 18 breaths a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.14,
      "end_seconds": 335.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Temperature 36.8, and oxygen saturation 95 per cent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.92,
      "end_seconds": 338.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Is that good?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.15,
      "end_seconds": 349.78,
      "duration_seconds": 9.63,
      "text": "It's acceptable, a little on the low side of comfortable. Lean forward and breathe in and out through your mouth for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.78,
      "end_seconds": 370.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.61,
      "text": "Like this? I did this at the clinic back home too, with a different doctor who had cold hands."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.16,
      "end_seconds": 382.71,
      "duration_seconds": 10.55,
      "text": "Just like that. I can hear a wheeze when you breathe out, on both sides, and your heart sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 383.87,
      "end_seconds": 387.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "That's the squeak I hear at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.01,
      "end_seconds": 392.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "So what is it, doctor? Be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.96,
      "end_seconds": 407.34,
      "duration_seconds": 13.38,
      "text": "I can't rule out asthma yet, even though it's late for it to start. With your smoking years I can't rule out COPD either. I'd rather test than guess."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.94,
      "end_seconds": 415.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "Well, test away. My mother would say better the devil you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 417.05,
      "end_seconds": 424.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "Then let's start with a breathing test called spirometry, here in the clinic, this week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 425.68,
      "end_seconds": 432.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "I'd also like a chest X-ray, to look at the lungs and heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 434.91,
      "end_seconds": 439.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Do I need to take my shirt off for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 441.81,
      "end_seconds": 450.71,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "Just the gown. I'd like some blood tests as well, to check for infection and your sugar levels."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 453.29,
      "end_seconds": 460.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.1,
      "text": "And we'll do an ECG, a quick heart tracing, before you leave today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 461.94,
      "end_seconds": 464.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Sounds like a spa day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 465.78,
      "end_seconds": 477.33,
      "duration_seconds": 11.55,
      "text": "Not quite, but near enough. In the meantime, Tanya, could you keep a note of when he wheezes at night?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 478.27,
      "end_seconds": 483.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Of course. I'll write it in his chart every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 484.43,
      "end_seconds": 492.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "Thank you. I'd like to see you both again in two weeks, once the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 493.68,
      "end_seconds": 499.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Two weeks. I'll miss bingo, no, that's Thursday. I'm fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 500.26,
      "end_seconds": 506.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "Then Thursday's safe. Anything else you want to ask before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 507.43,
      "end_seconds": 513.54,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "Only whether the shrimp thing is going to matter for any of this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 515.99,
      "end_seconds": 520.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "No, that's separate. Just keep avoiding it, Gene."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 520.98,
      "end_seconds": 525.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "I always do. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}
